      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "docs(config-channels): replace legacy allow:true with enabled:true for Discord, Slack, and Google Chat config examples",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSame pattern as [#102129](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/102129) and [#103491](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/103491). Config examples in `docs/gateway/config-channels.md` use `allow: true` for channel/group entries, but the strict Zod schemas only accept `enabled: true`.\n\n## Changes\n\n5 replacements across 3 channel sections in `docs/gateway/config-channels.md`:\n\n**Discord** (lines 278, 280):\n```diff\n-            general: { allow: true },\n+            general: { enabled: true },\n-              allow: true,\n+              enabled: true,\n```\n\n**Google Chat** (line 412):\n```diff\n-        \"spaces/AAAA\": { allow: true, requireMention: true },\n+        \"spaces/AAAA\": { enabled: true, requireMention: true },\n```\n\n**Slack** (lines 443, 446):\n```diff\n-        C123: { allow: true, requireMention: true, allowBots: false },\n+        C123: { enabled: true, requireMention: true, allowBots: false },\n-          allow: true,\n+          enabled: true,\n```\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Cmd:**\n```bash\ngrep -n \"{ allow: true\\|allow: true,\" docs/gateway/config-channels.md\n# (no matches after fix)\n```\n\nAll legitimate `allowFrom`, `allowBots`, `allowlist` fields are preserved unchanged.\n\n## Review\n\n- Manually reviewed and verified\n- AI-assisted: Yes\n",
